WEBVTT

00:10.530 --> 00:13.280
I'm glad you're safe, Lord Squale!

00:14.710 --> 00:16.000
It's been a while.

00:16.000 --> 00:19.260
We heard about your first deployment 
and came to lend a hand!

00:19.690 --> 00:20.480
Now...

00:22.040 --> 00:24.570
Let's return with tidings of victory!

00:32.050 --> 00:34.630
<b>Sweet Reincarnation</b>

01:58.560 --> 02:01.150
I'm so glad you're safe, Lord Squale.

02:02.290 --> 02:04.890
You saved me in my hour of need...

02:05.260 --> 02:07.210
There are no words to express my gratitude.

02:14.710 --> 02:20.880
<b>The Flavor of Consolation: Tarte Tatin</b>

02:14.890 --> 02:16.490
House Morteln?!

02:16.820 --> 02:18.530
Wretched Hubarek...

02:18.530 --> 02:21.660
He's even tamed a monster like that?

02:21.980 --> 02:24.510
With Morteln at their side,

02:24.510 --> 02:28.540
there's a chance Duke Kadlecek might 
send reinforcements after all.

02:31.740 --> 02:33.960
Should we withdraw our soldiers?

02:39.970 --> 02:42.700
Blast them all!

02:43.350 --> 02:45.850
Lord Squale, I'm so glad you're safe.

02:46.330 --> 02:50.810
I was beside myself with worry 
over my dear son-in-law.

02:51.050 --> 02:52.390
I'm so sorry.

02:52.390 --> 02:56.700
My lack of due diligence 
placed you in grave danger.

02:57.450 --> 02:59.150
The fault is not yours.

02:59.530 --> 03:01.940
And the two of you, I'm in your debt.

03:01.940 --> 03:03.370
You have my fondest gratitude!

03:04.220 --> 03:06.830
Lord Squale performed splendidly.

03:07.160 --> 03:10.860
Even surrounded by enemies, 
he refused to yield.

03:10.860 --> 03:13.320
He was determined to fight his way out.

03:14.810 --> 03:19.710
No. If you two hadn't come, I don't think...

03:20.800 --> 03:25.640
Lutoroute's army seems to have 
returned to its territory for now.

03:25.640 --> 03:27.510
That's excellent news.

03:27.890 --> 03:30.890
It's time to celebrate those 
with accomplishments in battle.

03:31.370 --> 03:35.480
First and foremost, Lord Squale's devotion.

03:35.480 --> 03:37.030
That's right.

03:38.380 --> 03:39.690
I hardly deserve it.

03:40.890 --> 03:42.920
You seem rather tired.

03:42.920 --> 03:44.140
It's understandable.

03:44.140 --> 03:46.290
You should rest for a while.

03:46.290 --> 03:48.190
I'll do that.

03:51.070 --> 03:52.370
Lord Squale!

03:52.780 --> 03:53.930
I'm so glad!

03:53.930 --> 03:55.330
You weren't hurt, were you?

03:56.970 --> 03:58.800
I appreciate your concern,

03:59.110 --> 04:01.870
but no more than scratches, I assure you.

04:02.340 --> 04:05.200
I'm truly glad you're safe.

04:10.720 --> 04:12.490
Lord Squale?

04:14.040 --> 04:17.130
I'm tired. We'll speak later.

04:17.460 --> 04:18.690
Then shall I show you to your room?

04:19.090 --> 04:20.430
I'm sorry.

04:20.430 --> 04:23.900
Please, let me be alone.

04:24.150 --> 04:25.540
Lord Squale?!

04:27.310 --> 04:30.090
I'm worried about the boy.

04:30.410 --> 04:32.920
Those with a painful first deployment

04:32.920 --> 04:37.290
sometimes find themselves crushed 
under the weight of the trauma.

04:37.290 --> 04:41.380
It does seem to have been difficult for him.

04:41.380 --> 04:42.490
It was.

04:42.490 --> 04:43.370
Of course,

04:43.370 --> 04:46.760
for the heir to the ducal house that 
oversees the royal capital's military,

04:46.760 --> 04:49.470
it's a necessary experience, but...

04:53.680 --> 04:57.230
But... that expression of his...

04:57.770 --> 04:59.370
I've never seen him like that before.

05:02.190 --> 05:05.900
What can I possibly do to aid him?

05:07.850 --> 05:13.010
Isn't there any way that I can comfort him?

05:14.610 --> 05:15.670
Pas.

05:15.670 --> 05:19.920
When we defeated those bandits, 
and Marc made his mistake,

05:19.920 --> 05:21.990
I recall you finding a way to comfort him.

05:23.880 --> 05:27.140
Oh... when I made the bonka pie?

05:27.980 --> 05:30.830
You're close in age to Lord Squale as well.

05:30.830 --> 05:32.300
Can you handle this?

05:32.300 --> 05:34.480
Me?

05:34.850 --> 05:37.310
Please, Lord Pastry.

05:37.310 --> 05:38.670
R-Right...

05:39.120 --> 05:44.780
<i>But if even Lady Petra can't 
comfort him, how could I?</i>

05:44.780 --> 05:50.110
There's nothing I want more than 
to see his brilliant smile again.

05:50.110 --> 05:51.740
Nothing more than that.

05:53.000 --> 05:53.850
Smile?

05:55.750 --> 05:58.920
If they could eat the finished 
desserts with a smile...

05:59.550 --> 06:05.260
Then everyone in the world 
could be happy and joyous!

06:05.860 --> 06:09.030
Sweets make everyone happy!

06:09.890 --> 06:12.100
<i>Behind every smile, there's a sweet!</i>

06:12.500 --> 06:13.500
Smile?

06:14.120 --> 06:15.970
Of course... smile!

06:16.210 --> 06:18.230
Looks like you've got an idea.

06:18.810 --> 06:20.760
There's something I want to make.

06:20.760 --> 06:22.940
Could you ready what I need?

06:23.660 --> 06:24.900
What kind of dessert is it?

06:24.900 --> 06:25.730
Wha?

06:26.050 --> 06:27.110
It's a dessert, right?

06:27.330 --> 06:28.810
Um, well...

06:28.810 --> 06:33.660
Father, I'm not doing this out of 
a personal desire to make sweets...

06:33.660 --> 06:35.000
Do whatever you like.

06:36.370 --> 06:37.450
Father!

06:37.750 --> 06:39.380
I'm leaving it in your hands.

06:39.380 --> 06:41.830
Lord Pastry, please!

06:42.170 --> 06:44.960
I'll see you get whatever you need.

06:44.960 --> 06:46.480
Thank you so much!

06:46.790 --> 06:49.430
Then could you ready some bonkas?

06:50.390 --> 06:51.530
Bonkas?

06:51.530 --> 06:53.390
Are you making bonka pie?

06:54.420 --> 06:55.250
No.

07:01.770 --> 07:07.780
<i>Lord Squale has shut himself away from 
the world because he feels incompetent.</i>

07:10.090 --> 07:13.200
<i>I want to bring him the light of a smile...</i>

07:13.770 --> 07:16.990
<i>The path back to happiness 
that a smile represents!</i>

07:29.590 --> 07:31.950
A toast to victory!

07:31.950 --> 07:33.260
To victory!

07:33.830 --> 07:36.350
This is our fief's best wine!

07:36.350 --> 07:38.210
Drink to your hearts' content!

08:05.670 --> 08:08.990
I thought it would be a long campaign, 
but it was just a minor skirmish?

08:08.990 --> 08:11.570
Yeah, I was hoping to get 
some recognition out of it.

08:11.570 --> 08:17.680
But the only one with any bragging 
rights is that spoiled little outsider!

08:17.680 --> 08:19.730
Nice work if you can get it, eh?

08:25.420 --> 08:27.150
Pay them no mind.

08:27.150 --> 08:29.060
They just want to complain.

08:29.580 --> 08:32.780
No... they're correct.

08:34.810 --> 08:38.640
It's unfortunate, but war 
comes with sacrifice.

08:39.370 --> 08:42.550
As the grandson of Duke Kadlecek,

08:42.550 --> 08:46.290
you must internalize that 
fact even more than most.

08:47.210 --> 08:48.750
You are correct.

08:49.210 --> 08:54.620
I've been given a position of prominence 
because of my place in the duke's line.

08:55.210 --> 08:58.760
The margrave even set up a perfect 
first campaign for me, and yet...

08:59.100 --> 09:02.600
I don't know how I'll face my grandfather.

09:03.010 --> 09:05.600
I struggled in my first campaign as well.

09:05.600 --> 09:08.610
You did well, Lord Squale.

09:08.610 --> 09:11.010
You're allowed to feel proud.

09:11.930 --> 09:13.500
Thank you for your kind words.

09:15.010 --> 09:16.530
<i>I can't get it out of my mind.</i>

09:17.570 --> 09:19.650
<i>All of them... because of my inexperience...</i>

09:26.810 --> 09:28.380
I'm sorry I'm late.

09:29.580 --> 09:34.170
Your Lordship, my most heartfelt 
congratulations on your victory.

09:34.170 --> 09:37.960
And you have my thanks for your 
aid provided from a distant land.

09:39.300 --> 09:40.950
And if I may say,

09:40.950 --> 09:45.320
your decisive, assertive, 
yet steady leadership

09:45.320 --> 09:47.990
does you credit as one of this 
kingdom's leading authorities.

09:47.990 --> 09:51.440
You're absolutely too kind! 
I don't know what to say.

09:51.760 --> 09:56.230
To celebrate the occasion, 
I briefly borrowed your kitchen.

09:56.230 --> 09:57.690
Might I reveal my creation?

09:57.690 --> 09:59.310
But of course!

10:29.850 --> 10:31.190
Is that...

10:32.250 --> 10:34.900
I can smell it from here! 
What a wonderful aroma!

10:35.510 --> 10:37.860
Is that a baked dessert?

10:38.690 --> 10:40.860
I've never seen anything like it!

10:46.380 --> 10:48.250
If you would, Lord Squale.

10:57.050 --> 10:59.540
<i>That reddish-brown stuff on top...</i>

10:59.540 --> 11:00.920
<i>Some kind of fruit?</i>

11:02.350 --> 11:04.210
What is this called?

11:04.520 --> 11:06.540
Tarte Tatin.

11:06.540 --> 11:08.600
Tarte... Tatin?

11:08.880 --> 11:10.890
It's a baked dessert made from bonkas.

11:10.890 --> 11:13.440
I made it for you.

11:14.010 --> 11:17.460
This part on top... it's bonkas?

11:17.460 --> 11:19.440
Baked bonkas?

11:19.440 --> 11:20.120
Yes.

11:20.780 --> 11:24.690
Nicolo, bring the tarte Tatin 
in the kitchen for the others.

11:24.690 --> 11:26.240
Yes, milord.

11:27.210 --> 11:29.730
<i>The fresh, sweet aroma of bonkas...</i>

11:29.730 --> 11:32.580
<i>The stimulating aroma of 
a freshly-baked crust...</i>

11:33.060 --> 11:34.200
<i>I can't help</i>

11:35.300 --> 11:37.160
<i>but feel hungry for that.</i>

11:42.580 --> 11:44.680
<i>These are... bonkas?</i>

11:44.680 --> 11:46.300
<i>It's so delicious!</i>

11:46.550 --> 11:51.390
The application of heat gives depth to the 
tartness and concentrates the sweetness.

11:51.820 --> 11:54.240
The crispness of the surface,

11:54.240 --> 11:55.980
the creaminess of the bonkas,

11:56.420 --> 11:58.700
and the crunchiness of the tart crust...

11:58.700 --> 12:00.750
The contrast between them is 
what makes it an amazing dish!

12:01.210 --> 12:04.950
I've never had such a 
delicious dessert before.

12:04.950 --> 12:06.220
I'm honored.

12:06.650 --> 12:08.340
Why is it called "tarte Tatin"?

12:08.900 --> 12:13.040
They say it comes from the master 
tart-makers, the Tatin sisters.

12:13.270 --> 12:14.780
Tatin sisters?

12:15.860 --> 12:20.460
Typically with tarts, you put fruit 
on top of the crust and bake.

12:20.460 --> 12:24.150
But one day, they forgot to 
put the crust into the mold,

12:24.150 --> 12:26.680
and ended up just baking the fruit.

12:27.440 --> 12:28.350
With no other choice,

12:28.350 --> 12:31.670
the sisters laid the crust on the 
half-baked fruit and let it finish.

12:33.080 --> 12:36.350
This tarte Tatin was the result.

12:36.350 --> 12:38.070
That's where it comes from?

12:38.070 --> 12:43.270
In other words, tarte Tatin comes 
from a failure at making tarts.

12:46.290 --> 12:48.330
A... failure?

12:50.690 --> 12:55.850
But I think this dessert is a 
wonderful, miraculous thing.

12:56.920 --> 12:58.040
Miraculous?

12:58.370 --> 13:00.970
Had the Tatin Sisters, 
upon realizing their failure,

13:00.970 --> 13:04.550
simply thrown out the 
fruit and started again,

13:04.970 --> 13:07.160
we might never have had tarte Tatin.

13:08.880 --> 13:11.790
A treat that most would've just thrown out...

13:11.790 --> 13:16.370
But because the sisters refused 
to let failure be the last word,

13:16.370 --> 13:18.980
we can enjoy its deliciousness now.

13:19.610 --> 13:23.440
Refused... to let failure be the last word?

13:23.840 --> 13:27.010
Whenever I mess up a sweet I'm making,

13:27.010 --> 13:29.530
I think back on the tarte Tatin.

13:29.780 --> 13:32.120
Failure isn't a waste at all.

13:32.600 --> 13:35.030
The important thing is that, even if you fail,

13:35.030 --> 13:37.600
you keep looking forward and working hard.

13:38.520 --> 13:42.130
<i>For the next heir to the Kadlecek name,
 failure is unacceptable!</i>

13:43.210 --> 13:44.800
Never show weakness!

13:45.210 --> 13:47.810
Remember, you are a leader!

13:48.440 --> 13:53.130
But... my failures aren't 
like most people's failures.

13:53.860 --> 13:56.500
You didn't fail, Lord Squale!

13:57.640 --> 13:59.310
Have you forgotten?

13:59.310 --> 14:03.360
What I said to you before you departed...

14:04.740 --> 14:07.800
<i>Please, return to me safely!</i>

14:09.630 --> 14:13.460
You kept your word to me.

14:13.460 --> 14:17.850
But... the only reason I made it back safe

14:17.850 --> 14:20.040
is because of the sacrifice 
of those under my leadership.

14:20.040 --> 14:23.750
I just feel... so awful for them.

14:23.750 --> 14:28.970
Isn't that how a leader should feel?

14:29.730 --> 14:32.930
Instead of celebrating the 
victory your first campaign,

14:33.490 --> 14:36.640
you're thinking about the 
men who died for you.

14:37.390 --> 14:42.400
I'm proud of you for your modesty.

14:43.460 --> 14:44.830
Lady Petra...

14:46.540 --> 14:52.410
Nothing could make me happier 
than having you back safely.

15:02.110 --> 15:04.210
Thank you, Lady Petra.

15:07.480 --> 15:09.670
Thank you, Lord Pastry.

15:10.010 --> 15:13.140
I'm going to become a stronger man.

15:13.910 --> 15:15.700
I won't let this failure be in vain.

15:16.890 --> 15:18.460
Lord Squale...

15:20.410 --> 15:23.970
Do you think... I can have another 
piece of the tarte Tatin?

15:23.970 --> 15:25.050
Of course!

15:26.030 --> 15:30.720
Lady Petra, would you like to enjoy this 
with me in a sunny part of the gardens?

15:31.160 --> 15:32.000
Yes.

15:34.390 --> 15:36.790
He seems to be in better spirits.

15:36.790 --> 15:37.760
Yes!

15:38.970 --> 15:43.270
The trauma of a first campaign is something 
you have to overcome on your own.

15:43.270 --> 15:46.960
I went through the same thing as a young man.

15:46.960 --> 15:48.510
Yes, that's right.

15:48.510 --> 15:51.720
I had many struggles 
myself when I was young!

15:51.720 --> 15:53.280
Oh, heavens...

15:53.280 --> 15:57.560
Still, Lord Pastry, I must
 offer you my thanks.

15:57.860 --> 16:01.030
If there's anything you wish, simply name it!

16:01.030 --> 16:03.020
Anything?!

16:03.020 --> 16:05.130
<i>But what I want...</i>

16:05.130 --> 16:09.010
<i>What I need to make my land of sweets...</i>

16:11.370 --> 16:14.200
Your Lordship, there's something
 I want very much!

16:21.770 --> 16:24.000
Welcome home, Pas!

16:24.000 --> 16:25.800
Yes, I've returned!

16:26.410 --> 16:28.160
Look at all that stuff!

16:28.160 --> 16:29.710
Are they merchants now?

16:30.080 --> 16:32.920
Expressions of gratitude from Lord Hubarek.

16:32.920 --> 16:34.680
I'm so glad you're safe!

16:35.010 --> 16:37.600
And your father gave me a letter for you!

16:38.070 --> 16:39.050
Oh!

16:39.420 --> 16:40.960
Thank you so much!

16:42.640 --> 16:45.190
"Work the negotiations to our benefit"?

16:45.430 --> 16:49.520
Is that why the boss 
stayed in the margravate?

16:49.520 --> 16:50.300
Yes.

16:51.220 --> 16:56.850
I'm going to make Baron Lunzvage 
pay for picking my pocket!

16:56.850 --> 16:59.960
He seemed pretty worked up.

16:59.960 --> 17:02.620
Like father, like son, huh?

17:02.620 --> 17:08.910
After all, this was all started 
with the baron buying up my goats

17:08.910 --> 17:11.840
while claiming he needed them as war provisions!

17:12.140 --> 17:15.490
I'm sure he won't complain if we buy 
up all the materials and livestock

17:15.490 --> 17:17.510
he was going to get in turn!

17:17.960 --> 17:19.300
Buy them up?

17:19.660 --> 17:24.010
After all, Morteln contributed 
the most to the campaign,

17:24.010 --> 17:27.830
so letting bygones be bygones with 
double what he took from us

17:27.830 --> 17:30.460
should help with other negotiations.

17:32.560 --> 17:34.890
That's a scary expression!

17:34.890 --> 17:37.060
Of course, it's up to Father—

17:37.060 --> 17:38.740
Negotiations are complete.

17:38.970 --> 17:39.890
Father!

17:39.890 --> 17:40.450
That was fast!

17:40.800 --> 17:41.470
C'mon.

17:42.170 --> 17:43.430
We're heading right back.

17:43.430 --> 17:45.370
What? Why?!

17:45.740 --> 17:48.340
It's going to take forever 
with my teleportation alone.

17:48.650 --> 17:51.680
It'll be faster if you replicate 
my magic and help carry it.

17:52.000 --> 17:54.130
I-Is there that much?

17:54.130 --> 17:56.670
Just what did you negotiate?

18:03.670 --> 18:05.480
Wh-Wh...

18:05.780 --> 18:07.940
What the heck is all this?!

18:08.520 --> 18:12.380
Boss! This is way too much!

18:12.380 --> 18:13.900
Look at these fine horses!

18:13.900 --> 18:17.530
They were going through checks 
before being shipped out,

18:17.530 --> 18:22.380
but I insisted they be sold to us before 
they were given to Baron Lunzvage.

18:22.380 --> 18:24.080
An eye for an eye?

18:24.440 --> 18:27.930
Apparently the baron paid a 
great amount of money in advance

18:27.930 --> 18:30.540
to have them raised from foals.

18:30.760 --> 18:34.260
To have a low-ranked noble 
swipe them from him...

18:34.260 --> 18:37.790
He's probably writhing 
in frustration about now.

18:37.790 --> 18:42.070
Boss, your face looks even
 scarier than the kid's.

18:44.320 --> 18:47.890
Hey, is this one of those wine things?

18:47.890 --> 18:49.730
A juicer?

18:50.190 --> 18:52.560
The more you turn this crank,

18:52.780 --> 18:54.600
the more the fruit inside gets crushed,

18:54.600 --> 18:56.650
and it forces the juice out.

18:57.840 --> 18:59.530
Let's try it out!

19:12.960 --> 19:15.240
Mother? You called?

19:15.240 --> 19:19.370
You need to go to the royal 
capital with Casserole!

19:19.370 --> 19:20.430
The royal capital?

19:20.430 --> 19:21.600
The truth is,

19:21.600 --> 19:24.290
my father's letter was inviting

19:24.290 --> 19:28.390
Petra and me to the royal 
capital at the end of summer.

19:28.390 --> 19:32.600
But I couldn't choose what to wear, 
so I wanted everyone's opinions...

19:32.600 --> 19:36.870
So we got together all the 
clothing in the house, but...

19:36.870 --> 19:39.820
None of them seem just right!

19:41.300 --> 19:44.690
I think we might have 
to prepare a new outfit,

19:44.690 --> 19:48.770
but there's no dressmaker in our fief 
worthy of clothing a noblewoman!

19:48.770 --> 19:51.070
You want to use a dressmaker 
in the capital, then?

19:51.420 --> 19:54.880
We'd like you to order a 
dress in Licorice's size.

19:54.880 --> 19:57.130
If we can just get the basic form made,

19:57.130 --> 19:59.380
we can embellish it on our own here.

19:59.380 --> 20:02.090
Can't Father handle that on his own?

20:02.090 --> 20:03.260
Absolutely not!

20:03.260 --> 20:07.730
Licorice doesn't want some 
man to know her dress size!

20:07.730 --> 20:09.450
I'm a man, too...

20:09.450 --> 20:11.810
Silence! You're her fiancé!

20:12.070 --> 20:14.040
Right, Licorice, dear?

20:14.430 --> 20:17.510
It's all right if... Pas knows.

20:17.510 --> 20:19.030
Goodness!

20:20.400 --> 20:22.590
R-Right!

20:22.590 --> 20:24.410
She's my fiancée, after all...

20:24.410 --> 20:26.490
That's right!

22:04.700 --> 22:07.390
<i>Father, are you well?</i>

22:08.010 --> 22:10.990
<i>It's been a month since 
my arrival in Morteln.</i>

22:11.720 --> 22:13.970
Are you baking something?

22:14.440 --> 22:16.930
It's what you've been waiting for.

22:19.750 --> 22:21.600
It smells wonderful!

22:21.600 --> 22:24.610
Cheesecake made from goat's milk.

22:25.330 --> 22:26.590
This is it?!

22:27.140 --> 22:31.130
<i>The sweets that Pas makes are like magic!</i>

22:33.240 --> 22:34.810
<b>SNORE</b>

22:34.450 --> 22:35.710
Hey!

22:36.480 --> 22:37.750
Sister!

22:37.750 --> 22:39.840
Everyone's waiting!

22:40.300 --> 22:41.740
Pas?

22:41.740 --> 22:43.470
Don't be such a brat.

22:43.470 --> 22:45.360
I can eat the cake here!

22:45.360 --> 22:46.650
Just bring i—

22:46.650 --> 22:48.720
Oh! Oh no! Lico?!

22:48.720 --> 22:50.690
How long were you watching?!

22:50.690 --> 22:52.650
Since you were asleep.

22:55.290 --> 22:57.890
<i>Everyone's being so kind to me.</i>

22:58.550 --> 23:00.820
<i>I'm having great fun every day.</i>

23:01.670 --> 23:03.050
<i>Regards, Licorice.</i>

23:03.750 --> 23:06.560
Oh, but I miss her!

23:08.400 --> 23:10.880
Pas, what are you making today?

